From 2170d56393191b4a5590556d6ce80d6a85943b7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bear <61359476+bearnl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:52:31 -0230
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc/powernv/rng: retry rng_create() from
 pnv_rng_late_init()

pnv_get_random_long_early() spends its single shot as soon as
slab_is_available(), but the first request for random bytes can arrive
from inside kmem_cache_init() itself: with CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_RANDOM
the freelist shuffle runs right after slab_state becomes UP and before
vmalloc_init().  rng_create() then fails in of_iomap(), both
ibm,power-rng nodes are dropped, ppc_md.get_random_seed is left NULL and
pnv_rng_late_init() creates no platform device.  On a POWER8 OpenPOWER
machine (no darn) the hardware RNG is therefore never initialised.

If something else populates the ibm,power-rng platform devices, for
example mtd_part_of_parse() calling of_platform_populate() with a NULL
node, the powernv-rng driver binds and dereferences the NULL per-CPU
pnv_rng pointer in pnv_get_random_long().

Retry rng_create() from pnv_rng_late_init() when the early attempt left
no seed hook, at which point ioremap() works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/rng.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/rng.c b/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/rng.c
index 196aa70fe..a0c7aa257 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/rng.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/rng.c
@@ -190,6 +190,11 @@ static int __init pnv_rng_late_init(void)
 	if (ppc_md.get_random_seed == pnv_get_random_long_early)
 		pnv_get_random_long_early(&v);
 
+	if (!ppc_md.get_random_seed) {
+		for_each_compatible_node(dn, NULL, "ibm,power-rng")
+			rng_create(dn);
+	}
+
 	if (ppc_md.get_random_seed == pnv_get_random_long) {
 		for_each_compatible_node(dn, NULL, "ibm,power-rng")
 			of_platform_device_create(dn, NULL, NULL);
-- 
